PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Colleagues split sharply: 10 favors E (Weak Quality Addition, arguing fixed α blocks existential high-welfare additions); 2/5/7/8/9/12 favor C (Non-Elitism, claiming CLU can rank tiny high-welfare additions over arbitrarily many near-c lives); 3/4/6/11 favor D (Weak Non-Sadism via Sadistic Conclusion). No support for A/B.  
Core facts preserved: Arrhenius sixth theorem pits exactly those five axioms; CLU ranks by Σ(w−c) with c>0. This immediately produces Sadistic Conclusion (some positive-but-sub-c additions worse than negative additions), violating Weak Non-Sadism while preserving additivity for Egalitarian Dominance, General Non-Extreme Priority, and Non-Elitism (sufficient near-c lives still dominate one very high life). Weak Quality Addition also holds once w≫c.  
Thus D is the unique violation; C and E rest on misapplications of the additive (w−c) structure. No corrections or new evidence yet; unresolved only why a minority mis-locates the conflict.}

